<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5806" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφίδῠμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>two-fold, double,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμένες ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.847
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκταί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.940
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάστιγγες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					2.179
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσθμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					6.1.5
				</span></i>
			; <i>of double nature,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				3.483
			</span></i>; <i>with two barbs,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.92
				</span></i>
			. (The termin. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δυμος</span> recurs
			in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίδυμος, τρίδυμος.</span>)</div>
